   "title": "How it works",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## OneShot MV: app\n\nThis workflow opens as an **app**: the settings on the right, the results in the middle. **App / Graph** at the top left switches to this node graph and back. It is the Voice workflow with the main settings shown and friendlier names.\n\n**One performance, many performers.** Load a song, write a World, click **Run**.\n\n**1. Preview first**\nLeave **Make the video** off and click **Run**. The Director:\n- analyses the song,\n- writes the World,\n- plans every shot.\n\n**The plan** lists every shot: time, energy, who, wearing what, and where. Nothing renders yet. Change the World line if you need to, turn **Make the video** on, and click **Run** again. The song analysis and the World are cached, so the second run starts faster.\n\n**2. The World (theme)**\nOne line is enough: *the gladiator games in ancient Rome*. It decides who the characters are, what they wear, the places, the light and the grade.\n\nFor more control, write three parts separated by semicolons: the people in the order you want them, then the places, then the light. For example: *the gladiator games in ancient Rome, all invented adults: a murmillo gladiator in a crested bronze helmet, a retiarius with a net and trident, the emperor in a purple toga ...; the sand of the packed Colosseum, the imperial box; hard midday sun*.\n\nThe characters you name are cast first, in that order (**cast_order** `as written`; `mixed` shuffles them). Every shot is a different person.\n\n**The edit**\nThe song is mapped into three energy levels, each cut its own way (**cuts_low / cuts_medium / cuts_high**):\n- **low** (the intro, quiet bridges): a cut every 2 bars.\n- **medium** (verses, builds): a cut every bar.\n- **high** (choruses, the drop): cuts to the music, each to a new face in the same spot.\n\n**audio_fx**: `subtle` (the default) adds flash, zoom, glow and colour split on the drums. `intense` is stronger and adds a motion-blurred twitch. `none` turns them off.\n\n**crowd**: `auto` puts a soft-focus crowd behind the singers when the World is a packed spectacle (an arena, a stadium, crowded stands); otherwise nobody else is in frame.\n\n**Take QC** checks every take and re-renders bad ones, at most doubling the render time. With the SyncNet weights installed (see the README), it also scores lip sync. A vision check looks at every picture before any video is made: one person, the right gender, no stray glasses or writing, period-right clothes.\n\n**broll_share**: about 1 shot in 8 becomes a cutaway where nobody sings, never on the drop. 0 turns it off.\n\nThe finished MP4 lands in `output/oneshot-mv/runs/<run>/final_<format>.mp4`.\n\n**Packs**\n- **crowd**: a new face every shot.\n- **eras**: invented archetypes through the decades.\n- **artist**: one singer from a photo. Un-bypass **Load Image**, pick the photo and set the pack to `artist`.\n\n**preset**: `quality` is LTX-2.3 in 3 stages at 50 fps; `fast` uses the same model at 25 fps with fewer steps.\n\n**seconds**: 0 renders the whole song. **start**: -1 picks the strongest stretch.\n\nUse music you have the rights to."
   ],
